LEMMA (proved, rigorous): aligned outlier scaling gives M(P u {w*m}) >= mu0*wm/(wm+pmax), monotone
up to mu0=M(P). So the far-element MIN lives at bounded m (finite check); the tail m>=m0 is >=1/13
whenever M(core) > 1/13 strictly. This is THM-726 Step 1 for ALIGNED lcm-carriers (the extremal MKs).
Non-aligned outliers (S101): M = M(core) CONSTANT (looser) -- also >= the aligned bound. Step 1 holds.
